  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want to delete an MP thread from the app, so that my MP list stays manageable as on the site.\n\n### Scope\n\n`DeletePrivateMessageFlow`: build the legacy request (fields traced to `MPListView.swift`), post with the selected account's session, classify the answer with LOT-037; never report success unless the answer proves it.\n\n- Module: HFRClient · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: FEATURES 'Not to lose': MP actions (delete); not covered by LOT-058 (mark unread, group members, MP quote)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `MPListView.swift:37-80` (`deleteTopic`, `modo/manageaction.php`, form-encoded POST)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-094-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-037 (#64, done)\n- LOT-041 (#67, done)\n- LOT-042 (#68, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nNothing: the captures #169 (delete answer) and #114 (list past the last page) are done in #400; every dependency above is done.\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N1 (#169): MP thread delete: the answer of `modo/manageaction.php` (legacy `MPListView.swift:37-80`) on success and on refusal, and the MP list right after\n- #114\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Request fields and order match the legacy code (cited) and the capture.\n- [ ] Success only on the captured success marker; refusal, logged-out and unknown answers are typed errors.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-094-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n",
